licans pulled $3 million reserved for ads against Cuellar, signaling the race has dropped off the GOP target list", "Cuellar holds a clear fundraising edge and led the only recent poll 45-34", "Prediction markets price Cuellar at roughly a 90 percent chance of winning", "The redrawn R+3 district and Trump's attacks on Cuellar leave some opening for Tijerina"], "rationale": "Every available signal points the same direction: most raters call it Lean D, markets price Cuellar near 90 percent, the lone August poll shows him up 11, and Republican advertisers have withdrawn their reservations against him. The redrawn R+3 seat and Trump's attacks keep this short of Safe, but the incumbent's money edge and durability make him clearly favored.", "watch": "If Republicans re-invest in paid advertising or Trump's attacks on Cuellar's character gain traction with South Texas's shifting Latino electorate, the margin could tighten meaningfully.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 53 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Henry Cuellar (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Nine-term incumbent Henry Cuellar, a conservative Democrat, seeks another term in a South Texas seat that was redrawn to lean Republican. He faces Webb County Judge Tano Tijerina, a former Democrat now running as a Trump-aligned Republican, along with a Green Party candidate. Independent raters mostly call the race Lean Democratic, and prediction markets give Cuellar roughly a 90 percent chance of holding the seat.\n\nCuellar leads in money, with $2.2 million raised and $1.1 million on hand to Tijerina's $1.4 million raised. The most recent public poll, from late August, showed Cuellar ahead 45 to 34. House Republicans recently pulled $3 million reserved for ads against him, a sign they see better opportunities elsewhere. Trump has attacked Cuellar's character despite having pardoned him, and South Texas's rightward drift gives Tijerina a plausible path, but the incumbent's moderate record and strong local standing make him the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9009, "margin": 7.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8779, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8804, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8627, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8617, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8968, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9013, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9125, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8966, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8974, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8927, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7979, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.838, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8528, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8529, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8187, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.8525, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8058, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.8372, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.8179, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.8733, "margin": 7.5}]}